@format 3
@title The Magic Rock
@start beach

@set polished = false
@set score = 0

:: beach
You find a dull grey rock on the sand.

if polished:
The rock gleams faintly in the afternoon sun.
else:
It's just an ordinary rock. Boring, even.
end

* Polish the rock -> beach [polished = true, score += 1]
* Throw it in the sea -> sea
* Put it in your pocket -> pocket [get rock]

:: sea
You hurl the rock into the waves. It sinks immediately.
Somewhere, a fish is disappointed.

Score: {score}
-> END

:: pocket
You put the rock in your pocket. It is a good rock.

Score: {score}
-> END

@format 3
@title Counter
@start start

@set n = 0
@set clicks = 0

:: start
The counter shows: {n}

You've pressed the button {clicks} {clicks == 1 | time | times}.

* Press the button [n += 1, clicks += 1]
* Reset [n = 0, clicks = 0]
* Stop -> END

@format 3
@title Parser Demo
@start hall
@parser
@ignore the a an

:: hall
A narrow hall. A DOOR is east, and a LAMP sits on a table.

* Look at the lamp | examine lamp, x lamp -> hall
* Take the lamp | get lamp, grab lamp -> hall [get lamp]
* Open the door | go east, east -> corridor

// Type "lamp" to see disambiguation. "help", "undo" and "save" work too.

:: corridor
You step through into a brighter corridor.

* Go back | west -> hall
* Continue -> END

@format 3
@title Tunnels and Once
@start gate

@set coins = 3
@list notes

// Consecutive lines form one paragraph. A blank line starts a new one.
// A line ending in a backslash is a hard line break.

:: gate #hub
The gate stands open. You have {coins} {coins == 1 | coin | coins}\
in your pocket.

>> weather

* Pick up the coin in the dirt -> gate [coins += 1, once]
* Read the sign -> sign
* Walk through -> END

// A passage called with >> is a snippet: text and effects only.
:: weather #snippet
{if coins > 3}The sun is out and the coins feel heavy.{else}Clouds gather over the gate.{end}

:: sign
[enter notes add sign]
[once coins += 1]
```
   _____________
  |  WELCOME    |
  |  TRAVELLER  |
  |_____________|
```

The sign is spotted with rust. Notes so far: {notes}.

* Back to the gate -> gate

@format 3
@title Hello, World
@start start

:: start
Hello, world!

This is a tgame — a tiny interactive story.

* Say goodbye -> END
* Say hello again -> start

@format 3
@title My Game
@author Your Name
@start start

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Welcome to tgame studio — format 3.
//
//     :: name              start a passage (a place)
//     plain text           narration; consecutive lines form a paragraph
//     (blank line)         new paragraph
//     * Label -> target    a choice that jumps to another passage
//     * Label [effect]     a choice that stays in place
//     * Label [once]       a choice that disappears after it is taken
//     ? question [var]     ask the player a question
//     ...                  pause half a second (or: ... 800, ... 2s)
//     ~type / ~normal      toggle the typewriter effect
//     [get X] [drop X]     inventory
//     if has X: ... end    check inventory
//     >> name              run another passage in place (a snippet)
//     @set x = 0           declare a variable
//     @list clues          declare a list
//     {variable}           insert a value into text
//     \-> or \*            escape: render as literal text
//
// Press ? for the full reference, or open an Example from the
// activity rail on the left to see a finished game.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@set score = 0

:: start
Replace this line with your opening paragraph.

* Go somewhere -> somewhere
* Finish here -> END

:: somewhere
You went somewhere. Congratulations!

Your score is {score}.

* Back to the start -> start
* Finish -> END

@format 3
@set n = 5
@set s = "a"
@list tags
:: a
[n += 2, n *= 3, n -= 1, n /= 4, n %= 3]
[s += "b", s += 1]
[n++]
[n--]
[n--]
[tags add one, tags add One, tags add two, tags remove ONE]
[get Lamp, get lamp, get key]
[drop LAMP]
n={n} s={s} tags={tags} inv={inventory} count={count tags}
{has key | key | nokey} {has lamp | lamp | nolamp} {tags has TWO | two | notwo}
-> END

